meta {
  name: Bulk assign
  type: http
  seq: 13
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/projects/{{projectId}}/issues/bulk-assign
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "issueIds": ["{{issueId}}"],
    "userIds": ["{{memberUserId}}"]
  }
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
}

docs {
  Workspace ADMIN or TEAM_LEADER on the project - rewriting a batch of other people's workload is
  a leader's call, unlike assigning a single issue. A DEVELOPER gets 403 FORBIDDEN.

  Additive: the listed people are added to every listed issue and nobody is taken off, so running
  it twice changes nothing. The response counts what happened - issuesTouched, assignmentsCreated,
  alreadyAssigned.

  Capped at 100 issues and 20 people per call. An issue belonging to another project is 404
  ISSUE_NOT_FOUND rather than quietly skipped.
}
